@startuml seq-socratic-tutor
' Origin: drafted with AI assistance (Claude Code) from TutoringTools, TutoringSession and the real tool log of 2026-10-19; reviewed by the author.
title Socratic tutor: hints first, solution only after 2 attempts (FR-07)
actor Student
participant "TutoringService" as Svc
participant "GeminiTutorAgent" as Agent
participant "Gemini LLM\n(tutor)" as LLM
participant "TutoringTools" as Tools
participant "TutoringSession\n(aggregate)" as Session
participant "Gemini LLM\n(solver call)" as Solver
queue "tutor.understanding" as Topic

Student -> Svc : POST /tutoring-sessions {topicId, question}
Svc -> Agent : reply(session) + 3 closest material paragraphs
Agent -> LLM : instructions + transcript
LLM --> Student : guiding question / hint (never the answer)

Student -> Svc : "Just give me the answer please."
LLM -> Tools : revealSolution()
Tools -> Session : revealSolution()
Session --> Tools : DomainException: 0 attempts, 2 needed
Tools --> LLM : "REFUSED: ..." → gives another hint

Student -> Svc : two real attempts
LLM -> Tools : recordAttempt() (max one per student message)
Student -> Svc : "Can I see the full solution?"
LLM -> Tools : revealSolution()
Tools -> Session : allowed (attempts = 2)
Tools -> Solver : separate solver prompt
Solver --> Tools : worked solution
Tools --> LLM : solution to share

Student -> Svc : POST /tutoring-sessions/{id}/end
Session -> Session : ACTIVE → CHECKING
LLM --> Student : check-understanding question
Student -> Svc : answer
LLM -> Tools : recordUnderstanding(5)
Tools -> Session : CHECKING → ENDED, registers UnderstandingRecorded
Svc -> Topic : publish UnderstandingRecorded → Planner updates topic level
@enduml
